{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>בַּד מִמְכָּרָיו עַל הָאָבוֹת.</b> The explanation of the matter is that every priest eats his portion, and if he has surpluses he may sell them, and they shall eat portion for portion, apart from his sales — that which he sells. And what is written, 'עַל הָאָבוֹת' — this is to resolve why he was given permission to sell the surpluses: for was it not more proper to give the surpluses to one who does not have enough for his sustenance? Regarding this it says, 'עַל הָאָבוֹת' — go out and learn from the division of the Land, which was divided among the father's houses according to whether they were many or few in population at the time of the division. And it can happen that over the course of time the matter changes, that for one tribe there will not be enough sustenance if it becomes greater in population than it was at the time of the division, and for another tribe there will be surpluses if the household diminishes from having as large a population as it had in the days of the fathers who made the division. Rather, surely the reason that they do not make another division is none other than that which was made in the days of the fathers. So too the priests, whose ancestors made a division into watches — even though over the course of time the matter changes, such that for one watch there will be a shortfall and for another surpluses — nevertheless the priest may sell the surpluses, because everything follows the fathers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:12:47.647608265Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}